EXT. ROOFTOP APIARY - GOLDEN HOUR

White hives in neat rows. A city skyline smolders behind them. Folding tables, paper lanterns, a rehearsal-dinner mood.

ANNELIESE VOSS (30s, beekeeper's veil pushed up) pours mead into small cups. JOSUE PEREIRA (30s, shirt sleeves rolled, hands scarred from hive tools) carries a tray of honeycomb. GRANDMOTHER FLORENCE (80s, cane, dressed for a wedding) sits at the head table. HIRO (30s, the groom, nervous tie) practices a toast under his breath. PETRA (30s, the bride's sister, sunglasses) watches Anneliese and Josue.

JOSUE
Mead?

ANNELIESE
Honeycomb?

He sets the tray down. She hands him a cup. Their fingers don't touch.

FLORENCE
(to the table)
Everyone sit. It's rude to stand while the bees work.

They sit. Hiro stands anyway.

HIRO
(clearing throat)
Thank you all for coming up here. To the bees.

PETRA
To the bees.

JOSUE
(dry)
To the bees.

ANNELIESE
(dry)
They never leave.

Josue lifts his cup. Anneliese does not. Petra's sunglasses angle toward her.

PETRA
Anneliese, something wrong with the mead?

ANNELIESE
No. Everything's perfect.

She sips. Josue sets his cup down, harder than he means to.

JOSUE
Seven years. You'd think I'd stop being surprised by what you won't say.

ANNELIESE
You'd think you'd stop assuming.

FLORENCE
(sharp)
Children.

HIRO
(to himself)
Oh no. Oh no, not the toast.

ANNELIESE
I wrote you a letter. Josue. I wrote you a hundred letters and I burned every one on this roof.

JOSUE
Then you burned the wrong thing.

A hive hums louder. Petra takes off her sunglasses. Florence drops her cane across the table with a clatter.

FLORENCE
Out. All of you. Let them finish.

Chairs scrape. Hiro scurries away. Petra hesitates, then follows. Anneliese and Josue stand alone among the hives.

ANNELIESE
(low)
You ruined my life.

JOSUE
You ruined mine first.

She steps close. He doesn't back away. Behind them the sun slides below the skyline.
